    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Question\n\nthere is a commit [feat(gr_clue)](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.clue/commit/378285270242fa23b441a68655d4af6cba8ac4c0)\r\n\r\nbasically, it added \r\n```\r\nlocal gr_clue = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' }\r\n    or { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = 'Virtual replace with character' }\r\n  local gr_clue_viz = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'x', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' } or {}\r\n\r\nreturn {\r\n    ...\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gq',     desc = 'Format text (operator)' },\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gR',     desc = 'Enter Virtual Replace mode' },\r\n    gr_clue,\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gs',     desc = 'Sleep' },\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gT',     desc = 'Go to previous tabpage' },\r\n    ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nthe problem is it shadows my local keybindings\r\n\r\nFor example, when I set a keybinding using \"gr\" to jump to a reference, like below, I will have to unnecessarily press one more key!\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set({ \"gr\", \"vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = \"References\", nowait = true})\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b3e3aae-4725-4841-be2b-a3fb3decc15e)\r\n\r\nIs there a way to turn this feature off?  I don't need a default **\"gr\"** key.\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">there is a commit <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.clue/commit/378285270242fa23b441a68655d4af6cba8ac4c0\">feat(gr_clue)</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">basically, it added</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local gr_clue = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' }\n    or { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = 'Virtual replace with character' }\n  local gr_clue_viz = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'x', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' } or {}\n\nreturn {\n    ...\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gq',     desc = 'Format text (operator)' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gR',     desc = 'Enter Virtual Replace mode' },\n    gr_clue,\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gs',     desc = 'Sleep' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gT',     desc = 'Go to previous tabpage' },\n    ...\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">local gr_clue = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' }\n    or { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = 'Virtual replace with character' }\n  local gr_clue_viz = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'x', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' } or {}\n\nreturn {\n    ...\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gq',     desc = 'Format text (operator)' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gR',     desc = 'Enter Virtual Replace mode' },\n    gr_clue,\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gs',     desc = 'Sleep' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gT',     desc = 'Go to previous tabpage' },\n    ...\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">the problem is it shadows my local keybindings</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example, when I set a keybinding using \"gr\" to jump to a reference, like below, I will have to unnecessarily press one more key!</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set({ &quot;gr&quot;, &quot;vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = &quot;References&quot;, nowait = true})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set({ \"gr\", \"vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = \"References\", nowait = true})\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/49930785/405767007-7b3e3aae-4725-4841-be2b-a3fb3decc15e.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..1qB6cynzbAq0_N4UJwvGuRKEHt8f0Wawr8yQ_c7YpXw\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/49930785/405767007-7b3e3aae-4725-4841-be2b-a3fb3decc15e.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..1qB6cynzbAq0_N4UJwvGuRKEHt8f0Wawr8yQ_c7YpXw\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to turn this feature off?  I don't need a default <strong>\"gr\"</strong> key.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nthere is a commit feat(gr_clue)\nbasically, it added\nlocal gr_clue = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' }\n    or { mode = 'n', keys = 'gr', desc = 'Virtual replace with character' }\n  local gr_clue_viz = vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 and { mode = 'x', keys = 'gr', desc = '+LSP' } or {}\n\nreturn {\n    ...\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gq',     desc = 'Format text (operator)' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gR',     desc = 'Enter Virtual Replace mode' },\n    gr_clue,\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gs',     desc = 'Sleep' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'gT',     desc = 'Go to previous tabpage' },\n    ...\n\nthe problem is it shadows my local keybindings\nFor example, when I set a keybinding using \"gr\" to jump to a reference, like below, I will have to unnecessarily press one more key!\nvim.keymap.set({ \"gr\", \"vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = \"References\", nowait = true})\n\n\nIs there a way to turn this feature off?  I don't need a default \"gr\" key.",
