            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> For example, when I set a keybinding using \"gr\" to jump to a reference, like below, I will have to unnecessarily press one more key!\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> vim.keymap.set({ \"gr\", \"vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = \"References\", nowait = true})\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThe core issue is not these clues but the fact that Neovim>=0.11 has all those four (at the moment) mappings built-in. So 'mini.clue' auto-detects them and treats user typing `gr` as if there might be next key (although mapping is done with `nowait = true` which 'mini.clue' doesn't really support when computing clues).\r\n\r\nThe solution here is to manually delete all those new built-in mappings:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'gri')\r\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'grr')\r\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'gra')\r\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'grn')\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example, when I set a keybinding using \"gr\" to jump to a reference, like below, I will have to unnecessarily press one more key!</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set({ &quot;gr&quot;, &quot;vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = &quot;References&quot;, nowait = true})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set({ \"gr\", \"vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = \"References\", nowait = true})\n</code></pre></div>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The core issue is not these clues but the fact that Neovim&gt;=0.11 has all those four (at the moment) mappings built-in. So 'mini.clue' auto-detects them and treats user typing <code class=\"notranslate\">gr</code> as if there might be next key (although mapping is done with <code class=\"notranslate\">nowait = true</code> which 'mini.clue' doesn't really support when computing clues).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The solution here is to manually delete all those new built-in mappings:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.del('n', 'gri')\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'grr')\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'gra')\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'grn')\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">del</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>gri<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">del</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>grr<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">del</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>gra<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">del</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>grn<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "For example, when I set a keybinding using \"gr\" to jump to a reference, like below, I will have to unnecessarily press one more key!\nvim.keymap.set({ \"gr\", \"vim.lsp.buf.references, desc = \"References\", nowait = true})\n\n\nThe core issue is not these clues but the fact that Neovim>=0.11 has all those four (at the moment) mappings built-in. So 'mini.clue' auto-detects them and treats user typing gr as if there might be next key (although mapping is done with nowait = true which 'mini.clue' doesn't really support when computing clues).\nThe solution here is to manually delete all those new built-in mappings:\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'gri')\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'grr')\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'gra')\nvim.keymap.del('n', 'grn')",
